 - The engine's `start()` method rejects the returned promise when it cannot bind the configured port, rather than emitting an unhandled error event that would take the process down ([validated by: rejects instead of taking the process down with an unhandled error event](../../src/config.test.ts#L174)).
 
+## When beforeSession throws
+
+- When `beforeSession` throws an `Error`, the rejection still reaches the caller, and `onError` fires with the session and error just as for any other orchestrator failure ([validated by: fires onError with the session and error and still rejects when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionFailure.acceptance.test.ts#L35)).
+- When `beforeSession` throws, `afterSession` still runs after `onError` while no turn-body hook (`beforeUserInput`, `afterUserInput`, `beforeModelResponse`, `afterModelResponse`) or provider call has run, so `afterSession` cleanup hooks must not assume `beforeSession` succeeded ([validated by: fires afterSession after onError without starting the turn when beforeSession throws](../../src/orchestration/beforeSessionFailure.acceptance.test.ts#L60)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
 These three properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
